{"name":"Asbravn","status":"ok","title":"Asbravn","pageId":43809,"html":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p class=\"mw-empty-elt\">\n</p><aside role=\"region\" class=\"portable-infobox pi-background pi-border-color pi-theme-frwiki pi-layout-default type-location\">\n\n\n<h2 class=\"pi-item pi-item-spacing pi-title pi-secondary-background\" data-source=\"name\">Asbravn</h2>\n<section class=\"pi-item pi-group pi-border-color\">\n\t<h2 class=\"pi-item pi-header pi-secondary-font pi-item-spacing pi-secondary-background\">Geography</h2>\n\n<div class=\"pi-item pi-data pi-item-spacing pi-border-color\" data-source=\"region\">\n\t\n\t\t<h3 class=\"pi-data-label pi-secondary-font\">Region</h3>\n\t\n\t<div class=\"pi-data-value pi-font\">Between <a href=\"/wiki/Dusk_Road\" title=\"Dusk Road\">Dusk Road</a> and the <a href=\"/wiki/Uldoon_Trail\" title=\"Uldoon Trail\">Uldoon Trail</a><sup id=\"cite_ref-VGttSC.p148-149,213_1-0\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-VGttSC.p148-149,213-1\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>1<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup></div>\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"pi-item pi-data pi-item-spacing pi-border-color\" data-source=\"size\">\n\t\n\t\t<h3 class=\"pi-data-label pi-secondary-font\">Size</h3>\n\t\n\t<div class=\"pi-data-value pi-font\">Small Town</div>\n</div>\n\n</section>\n<section class=\"pi-item pi-group pi-border-color\">\n\t<h2 class=\"pi-item pi-header pi-secondary-font pi-item-spacing pi-secondary-background\">Society</h2>\n\n<div class=\"pi-item pi-data pi-item-spacing pi-border-color\" data-source=\"religion\">\n\t\n\t\t<h3 class=\"pi-data-label pi-secondary-font\">Religions</h3>\n\t\n\t<div class=\"pi-data-value pi-font\"><a href=\"/wiki/Ilmater\" title=\"Ilmater\">Ilmater</a>, <a href=\"/wiki/Lliira\" title=\"Lliira\">Lliira</a>, <a href=\"/wiki/Lathander\" title=\"Lathander\">Lathander</a>, <a href=\"/wiki/Waukeen\" title=\"Waukeen\">Waukeen</a><sup id=\"cite_ref-VGttSC.p148-149,213_1-1\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-VGttSC.p148-149,213-1\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>1<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup></div>\n</div>\n\n</section>\n<nav class=\"pi-navigation pi-item-spacing pi-secondary-font\"><a href=\"/wiki/Category:Inhabitants_of_Asbravn\" title=\"Category:Inhabitants of Asbravn\">Inhabitants of  Asbravn</a></nav>\n<nav class=\"pi-navigation pi-item-spacing pi-secondary-font\"><a href=\"/wiki/Category:Locations_in_Asbravn\" title=\"Category:Locations in Asbravn\">Locations in  Asbravn</a></nav>\n<nav class=\"pi-navigation pi-item-spacing pi-secondary-font\"><a href=\"/wiki/Category:Organizations_in_Asbravn\" title=\"Category:Organizations in Asbravn\">Organizations in  Asbravn</a></nav>\n</aside>\n\n<p class=\"mw-empty-elt\"></p><p><b>Asbravn</b> (<small><span style=\"font-variant: small-caps;\">pronounced</span>:&#160;/<a href=\"/wiki/A_as_in_%22bard%22\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"A as in &quot;bard&quot;\">ɑː</a><a href=\"/wiki/Z_as_in_%22wizard%22\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Z as in &quot;wizard&quot;\">z</a>ˈ<a href=\"/wiki/B_as_in_%22bard%22\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"B as in &quot;bard&quot;\">b</a><a href=\"/wiki/R_as_in_%22ranger%22\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"R as in &quot;ranger&quot;\">r</a><a href=\"/wiki/A_as_in_%22bard%22\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"A as in &quot;bard&quot;\">ɑː</a><a href=\"/wiki/V_as_in_%22vision%22\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"V as in &quot;vision&quot;\">v</a><a href=\"/wiki/E_as_in_%22elf%22\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"E as in &quot;elf&quot;\">ɛ</a><a href=\"/wiki/N_as_in_%22dragon%22\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"N as in &quot;dragon&quot;\">n</a>/&#160;<i>az-BRAH-ven</i><sup id=\"cite_ref-FRCS1e-CR-p26_2-0\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-FRCS1e-CR-p26-2\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>2<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup></small>) was a small town found in the <a href=\"/wiki/Western_Heartlands\" title=\"Western Heartlands\">Western Heartlands</a>.<sup id=\"cite_ref-VGttSC.p148-149,213_1-2\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-VGttSC.p148-149,213-1\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>1<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup>\n</p>\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\"><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Geography\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Geography</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Description\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Description</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Activities\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Activities</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Defenses\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Defenses</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Notable_Locations\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Notable Locations</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Inns_&_Taverns\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Inns &amp; Taverns</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Shops\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Shops</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Appendix\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Appendix</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#References\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">References</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Geography\">Geography</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a title=\"Edit section: Geography\" class=\"mw-editsection-visualeditor\" data-tracking-label=\"edit-section-anon\" data-action=\"edit-section\" href=\"https://forgottenrealms.fandom.com/wiki/Asbravn?veaction=edit&section=1\" aria-label=\"Edit section: Geography\"></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Asbravn lay in a shallow valley in between the <a href=\"/wiki/Dusk_Road\" title=\"Dusk Road\">Dusk Road</a> and the <a href=\"/wiki/Uldoon_Trail\" title=\"Uldoon Trail\">Uldoon Trail</a>.<sup id=\"cite_ref-VGttSC.p148-149,213_1-3\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-VGttSC.p148-149,213-1\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>1<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Description\">Description</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a title=\"Edit section: Description\" class=\"mw-editsection-visualeditor\" data-tracking-label=\"edit-section-anon\" data-action=\"edit-section\" href=\"https://forgottenrealms.fandom.com/wiki/Asbravn?veaction=edit&section=2\" aria-label=\"Edit section: Description\"></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Asbravn had lush farms, wood lots, well-kept barns, drainage ditches, ponds, and an air of tranquility.<sup id=\"cite_ref-VGttSC.p148-149,213_1-4\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-VGttSC.p148-149,213-1\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>1<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup> \n</p><p>A dilapidated temple to <a href=\"/wiki/Ilmater\" title=\"Ilmater\">Ilmater</a> faced the market, which was ringed by swap shops, a cooper and cratemaker, a wagonworks. The town also included shrines to <a href=\"/wiki/Lliira\" title=\"Lliira\">Lliira</a>, <a href=\"/wiki/Lathander\" title=\"Lathander\">Lathander</a> and <a href=\"/wiki/Waukeen\" title=\"Waukeen\">Waukeen</a> though the later was  abandoned by priests and was used as a playground by children. The <span class=\"new\" title=\"Tankard and Sheaf (page does not exist)\" data-uncrawlable-url=\"L3dpa2kvVGFua2FyZF9hbmRfU2hlYWY/YWN0aW9uPWVkaXQmcmVkbGluaz0x\">Tankard and Sheaf</span> was a popular tavern and the <a href=\"/wiki/Board_Laid_Bare_(Asbravn)\" title=\"Board Laid Bare (Asbravn)\">Board Laid Bare</a> was a local inn.<sup id=\"cite_ref-VGttSC.p148-149,213_1-5\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-VGttSC.p148-149,213-1\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>1<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Activities\">Activities</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a title=\"Edit section: Activities\" class=\"mw-editsection-visualeditor\" data-tracking-label=\"edit-section-anon\" data-action=\"edit-section\" href=\"https://forgottenrealms.fandom.com/wiki/Asbravn?veaction=edit&section=3\" aria-label=\"Edit section: Activities\"></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The town served as the market center of the southern Vale farmers. Here, they did their trading with each other and with traveling merchants from the cities, where others made a profit from their food. Buyers from <a href=\"/wiki/Berdusk\" title=\"Berdusk\">Berdusk</a> and <a href=\"/wiki/Iriaebor\" title=\"Iriaebor\">Iriaebor</a> came to the market each day. It was a common rumor that the market of Asbravn filled bellies all along the <a href=\"/wiki/Chionthar\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Chionthar\">Chionthar</a>.<sup id=\"cite_ref-VGttSC.p148-149,213_1-6\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-VGttSC.p148-149,213-1\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>1<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup>\n</p><p>Another not-quite-so troubling event was that a farmer was planning to breed long-horned <a href=\"/wiki/Horse\" title=\"Horse\">horses</a>. The only relic of its long past was an old, stout, cracked stone pillar, surmounted by crumbling horse heads. This pillar came from when the town was a city, <span class=\"new\" title=\"Urdrath (page does not exist)\" data-uncrawlable-url=\"L3dpa2kvVXJkcmF0aD9hY3Rpb249ZWRpdCZyZWRsaW5rPTE=\">Urdrath</span> of the Horsemen. The Horsemen moved from <span class=\"new\" title=\"Tunland (page does not exist)\" data-uncrawlable-url=\"L3dpa2kvVHVubGFuZD9hY3Rpb249ZWRpdCZyZWRsaW5rPTE=\">Tunland</span> long ago when they were nomads. Urdrath buried their dead in catacombs beneath the streets where unwary people now pass.<sup id=\"cite_ref-VGttSC.p148-149,213_1-7\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-VGttSC.p148-149,213-1\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>1<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Defenses\">Defenses</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a title=\"Edit section: Defenses\" class=\"mw-editsection-visualeditor\" data-tracking-label=\"edit-section-anon\" data-action=\"edit-section\" href=\"https://forgottenrealms.fandom.com/wiki/Asbravn?veaction=edit&section=4\" aria-label=\"Edit section: Defenses\"></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The <a href=\"/wiki/Riders_in_Red_Cloaks\" title=\"Riders in Red Cloaks\">Riders in Red Cloaks</a>, police and defenders, were well-known. A few experienced warriors, occasionally bolstered by mages and priests, and local volunteers were sponsored by Iriaebor to safeguard the market and surrounding roads. They patrolled in mounted dozens and often had to battle bandits, trolls, orcs, bugbears and predatory monsters in the southern <a href=\"/wiki/Sunset_Mountains\" title=\"Sunset Mountains\">Sunset Mountains</a>.<sup id=\"cite_ref-VGttSC.p148-149,213_1-8\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-VGttSC.p148-149,213-1\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>1<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup> \n</p><p>The <a href=\"/wiki/Zhentarim\" title=\"Zhentarim\">Zhentarim</a> gave the Cloaks a hard time with poisonings and well-paid mercenary ambushes. In almost every family, there was one who was chosen to be a Rider. Once, they offered a post to any warrior, with archers being particularly sought after. They got a pay rate of ten gold pieces per week. After a while, Abject Supplicant <a href=\"/wiki/Asgar_Tellendar\" title=\"Asgar Tellendar\">Asgar Tellendar</a> started insisting on questioning applicants with the aid of the <a href=\"/wiki/Harpers\" title=\"Harpers\">Harpers</a>.<sup id=\"cite_ref-VGttSC.p148-149,213_1-9\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-VGttSC.p148-149,213-1\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>1<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Notable_Locations\">Notable Locations</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a title=\"Edit section: Notable Locations\" class=\"mw-editsection-visualeditor\" data-tracking-label=\"edit-section-anon\" data-action=\"edit-section\" href=\"https://forgottenrealms.fandom.com/wiki/Asbravn?veaction=edit&section=5\" aria-label=\"Edit section: Notable Locations\"></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Asbravn was known for its shearing-market, which was a major producer of raw <a href=\"/wiki/Wool\" title=\"Wool\">wool</a> for nearby <a href=\"/wiki/Berdusk\" title=\"Berdusk\">Berdusk</a>'s wool industry.<sup id=\"cite_ref-FRA-p78_3-0\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-FRA-p78-3\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>3<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup>\n</p>\n<h3><span id=\"Inns_.26_Taverns\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Inns_&_Taverns\">Inns &amp; Taverns</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a title=\"Edit section: Inns & Taverns\" class=\"mw-editsection-visualeditor\" data-tracking-label=\"edit-section-anon\" data-action=\"edit-section\" href=\"https://forgottenrealms.fandom.com/wiki/Asbravn?veaction=edit&section=6\" aria-label=\"Edit section: Inns & Taverns\"></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<ul><li>The <a href=\"/wiki/Board_Laid_Bare_(Asbravn)\" title=\"Board Laid Bare (Asbravn)\">Board Laid Bare</a><sup id=\"cite_ref-VGttSC.p152_4-0\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-VGttSC.p152-4\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>4<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup></li>\n<li>The <span class=\"new\" title=\"Tankard and Sheaf (page does not exist)\" data-uncrawlable-url=\"L3dpa2kvVGFua2FyZF9hbmRfU2hlYWY/YWN0aW9uPWVkaXQmcmVkbGluaz0x\">Tankard and Sheaf</span><sup id=\"cite_ref-VGttSC.p152_4-1\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-VGttSC.p152-4\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>4<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup></li></ul>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Shops\">Shops</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a title=\"Edit section: Shops\" class=\"mw-editsection-visualeditor\" data-tracking-label=\"edit-section-anon\" data-action=\"edit-section\" href=\"https://forgottenrealms.fandom.com/wiki/Asbravn?veaction=edit&section=7\" aria-label=\"Edit section: Shops\"></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/Rolling_Wheel_Wagons\" title=\"Rolling Wheel Wagons\">Rolling Wheel Wagons</a><sup id=\"cite_ref-VGttSC.p151_5-0\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-VGttSC.p151-5\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>5<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup></li>\n<li><span class=\"new\" title=\"Samborl's Sundries-in-Trade (page does not exist)\" data-uncrawlable-url=\"L3dpa2kvU2FtYm9ybCUyN3NfU3VuZHJpZXMtaW4tVHJhZGU/YWN0aW9uPWVkaXQmcmVkbGluaz0x\">Samborl's Sundries-in-Trade</span><sup id=\"cite_ref-VGttSC.p150_6-0\" class=\"reference\"><a href=